\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The nine models. Every model uses the same PPO and LSTM backbone and the same object-relative push primitive; only the reward and the training dynamics change. The seed column gives the number of random seeds behind each model's headline confidence interval, taken at 528 environments. The single-agent Baseline and PBRS are trained across 256, 512, 1{,}024, 2{,}048, and 528 environments, with three seeds per swept count and five at the 528 anchor. The self-play subjects ASP-dPose and TASP-dPose are additionally trained at 256 and 2{,}048 environments, with three seeds, so that the single-GPU compute budget can be tested, rather than assumed, as a cause of the underperformance. The component ablations use three seeds and the gym runs a single seed; the full per-phase counts are given in Section~\ref {sec:experiment-set} and Chapter~\ref {sec:experiments}.}}{26}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:models}{{1}{26}{}{}{}}
